# Plan Adherence

Before implementing any feature, creating any file, or adding any dependency, verify it
traces to the approved product plan.

## Feature Scope

All implementation work must map to an approved feature in `docs/feature-list.md`:

| Feature | Scope |
|---------|-------|
| F1 | METAR → IWXXM conversion |
| F2 | IWXXM validation |
| F3 | Airport data services |
| F4 | IWXXM version handling |
| M1 | Monorepo layout (`apps/` + `packages/` + `vendor/`) |
| M2 | Vendor snapshot sync (wmo-im iwxxm-*) |
| M3 | GIFTs as in-repo package |
| M4 | Auth merged into backend API |
| M5 | Workspace tooling (uv + pnpm + Makefile) |
| M6 | Vendor upstream sync (wmo-im iwxxm-*) |

If work does not map to an approved feature, raise `[Scope Drift]` via AskQuestion:
- Cite the code or file being created
- Explain which feature it was intended for
- First option: "Map to feature FN — here's why..."
- Last option: "Let me explain / provide more context"

### Out of Scope (do not implement)

Document permanent exclusions in `docs/spec.md` §Non-Goals and `docs/feature-list.md`.
Do not implement capabilities listed there without an evolve cycle (16-evolve).

**Migration non-goal (REQ-016)**: No product feature rewrites during monorepo migration.
Structural moves and wiring only — behavior of F1–F4 must remain unchanged.

## Component Verification

New files must map to an approved component from `docs/spec.md` §Component Overview:

| Component | Location |
|-----------|----------|
| Backend API | `apps/backend/` |
| Frontend | `apps/frontend/` |
| E2E workspace | `apps/e2e/` |
| Auth library | `packages/auth/` |
| GIFTs | `packages/gifts/` |
| Shared | `packages/shared/` |
| Vendor schemas | `vendor/schemas/*` (read-only) |

Files outside approved locations require justification. Raise `[Scope Drift]` if a new
component is introduced that is not in the spec.

During migration, legacy paths (`backend/`, `frontend/`, `GIFTs/`, `auth/`, `schemas/`)
are transitional only — new work targets the monorepo tree above.

## Dependency Verification

Before adding any new dependency, check `docs/dependency-inventory.md`. If the dependency
is not listed:
1. Raise `[Decision]` with a recommendation
2. On approval, back-add to `docs/dependency-inventory.md`
3. Record the decision in `workflow-state.yaml` §`decisions_log`

## Browser Connectivity

Frontend-facing API changes must trace to connectivity tasks in the execution plan and
`docs/test-plan.md` tiers H4–H5. See [connectivity-gates.md](../../skills/connectivity-gates.md).
